        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "05db304d-d045-5a47-bb30-eb707b938af0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Croydon Airport, Gatwick Airport, Northolt Aerodrome, London Heathrow Airport, Brussels-Evere Airport, South London, south-east England, Crawley, Central London\n- Products: 1921 SNETA Farman Goliath\n- Concepts: airport identifiers, airport traffic ranking, mail flights\n\nFacts:\n- Croydon Airport was an airport in South London, England, with ICAO code EGCR.\n- Croydon Airport was the main airport for London before Northolt Aerodrome, London Heathrow Airport, and Gatwick Airport replaced it.\n- A 1921 SNETA Farman Goliath operated a mail flight from Croydon Airport in the United Kingdom to Brussels-Evere Airport in Belgium.\n- Gatwick Airport, also known as London Gatwick, is a major international airport in south-east England, 29.5 miles south of Central London and 2.7 nautical miles north of Crawley.\n- Gatwick Airport has IATA code LGW and ICAO code EGKK.\n- Gatwick Airport is the eighth-busiest airport in Europe.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
